  pages={935-939},
  abstract={In the evolving landscape of the Internet of Drones (IoD), securing touchy and assignment-vital facts is paramount because of the wider assault floor and stringent electricity constraints specific to IoD networks. This paper introduces “IoD-Crypt,” a completely specific cryptographic framework engineered to address those traumatic situations by offering a strong, strength-inexperienced answer tailored for battery-confined IoD packages. Leveraging specialized precomputation strategies and self-certified cryptographic primitives, IoD-Crypt achieves notable computation and conversation efficiencies. By circumventing the rules of latest public key cryptography suites, the framework guarantees a immoderate stage of protection inside the random oracle model. Through complete implementations on everyday drone processors, which consist of eight-bit AVR and 32-bit ARM, IoD-Crypt demonstrates an remarkable reduce rate in energy consumption, as lots as forty eight times lower than conventional techniques. This massive development paves the manner for at ease, sustainable IoD operations, emphasizing the framework’s capability for big adoption and trying out.},
  keywords={Energy consumption;Program processors;Reviews;Oral communication;Public key cryptography;Cryptography;Internet of Things;Internet of Drones;Drone Security;Network Security;Public Key Cryptography;Lightweight Cryptography},
