  title={Transnomous: Automated Accident Detection and Reporting System}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-5},
  abstract={Saving lives is a never-ending mission to help others. Individuals suffer because of accidents, and some people die because of them. If the victims use the alert system to warn their loved ones, it can save lives and support them in every way imaginable. This system recognizes the accident through various inputs, such as a vibration sensor detecting any sudden shaking on the vehicle, and when the car is tilted through certain angles from its original location, the accelerometer sensor senses it. Through the GSM Module, the alert system sends the signal to the AVR controller, then it sends the message with the accident location to pre-programmed numbers like ambulance, police station, loved ones, etc. This idea is also to alert the drivers about such zones (School/Hospital/Police) to avoid accidents in school areas, to keep quiet in the hospital area. This system consists of a Zone status unit and Speed display and Control unit. Once the information is received from the zones, the bike's embedded unit automatically alerts the driver, to reduce the speed according to the zone, it waits for few second, then if the bike is in the speed limit and the bike's speed is still not reduced below that speed limit, the number of the bike and the owners detailed will be sent to RTO (we have assumed a third party) through SMS.},
  keywords={Vibrations;Accelerometers;Hospitals;Smart cities;Law enforcement;Velocity control;Message services;Road safety;Accidents;Vehicles;Accident detection;Smart alert system;Emergency message;Location tracking;Vibration sensor;Accelerometer;Speed control;Accident prevention;Safe driving;Authorities notification},
